{"document_id": "209bab0e-fa03-4c50-9251-330730882e88", "crop": "mango", "organization": "TNAU", "source": "TNAU", "source_url": "https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/crop_prot_postharvest_mango_2.html", "title": "TNAU Agritech Portal :: Crop Protection", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-06T23:40:53.383011", "content": "| ![TNAU Agritech Portal](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/index/cp_index.jpg)  |  \n| --- |  \n|  [Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmer's Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\")  |   |  \n|  Post Harvest Diseases :: Fruits :: Mango  \n |  **Stem End Rot:_Lasiodiplodia theobromae_** **Symptoms**\n  * In fruits, the pericarp darkens near the base of the pedicel.\n  * The affected area enlarges to form a circular, black patch which under humid atmosphere extends rapidly and turns the whole fruit completely black within two or three days.\n  * The pulp becomes brown and softer.\n\n  \n | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/2.Mango%20stem%20end%20rot2.JPG)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/stem_end_rot_3.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/stem_end_rot_4.jpg)  | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/stem_end_rot_2.jpg)  |  \n| --- | --- | --- | --- |  \n| **Darken pericarp**  | **Circular black patch**  | **severe infection**  | **Infected fruits**  |  \n**Management**  \n\n  * Avoid harvesting immature fruit. Postharvest treatment with hot water and carbendazim (Spin Flo) is partially effective against stem end rot.\n  * For control of stem end rot during controlled atmosphere storage, a dual treatment of hot carbendazim (Spin Flo) followed by prochloraz is necessary.\n  * Fruit from orchards with a history of stem end rot losses should be rejected for long term storage. The severity of stem end rot can be assessed as follows.\n  * Harvest 100 mature fruit at random from throughout the orchard.\n  * Leave them untreated and store at 25° until they are fully ripe. Ideally, less than one-tenth and certainly no more than one-third of the fruit should develop symptoms of stem end rot by the time they are fully ripe.\n\n\nImage Source:\n<https://www.apsnet.org/publications/imageresources/Pages/tropical087.aspx>  \n<http://www.abc.net.au/site-archive/rural/nt/content/201210/s3604875.htm>[  \n](http://www.abc.net.au/site-archive/rural/nt/content/201210/s3604875.htm)\nS Iram and HMI Ahmad. Major Post Harvest Disease of Mango and their Management. 2013. _Intl. J. Agron. Plant. Prod._**4 (12),** pp: 3470-3484. \n |  \n |  \n| \n* * *\n[Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmers Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact Us ](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\") © 2015 TNAU. All Rights Reserved.  |\n", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\"><html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><head>\n<meta http-equiv=